  "description": "SIKYIX crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C92 H124 Dy4 Fe2 N2 O30. From the CIF bond table, Fe1 (Fe) has 6 O neighbors; Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Fe2 (Fe) has 6 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 7 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately linear metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.209-3.583 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 95.03-106.70°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C92H124Fe2Dy4N2O30. Article name explicitly identifies I(II).",
